      "content": "but that's just subjective bias. i'm talking about the actual logic of it. if the outcome of living and the outcome of not living are both zero—meaning no ultimate purpose or permanent impact—then choosing to end it isn't \"sad,\" it's just a neutral decision to stop an unnecessary process. it's like choosing to turn off a machine that isn't producing anything. wouldn't you agree that's the most rational way to look at it?",
